<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico competes liquidity drain.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico competes liquidity drain.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico drained 3.034 billion pesos from the secondary market on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>It sold Cetes directly as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    337 days   23.08 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    176 days   22.12 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     85 days   21.41 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of its repurchase agreements were as follows:</p>
<p>    600 million     37 days   20.30 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     26 days   20.25 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     16 days   20.14 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     12 days   20.15 pct</p>
<p>    184 million	1 day    20.04 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Elena Vega, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9554))</p>
</text>
